# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Personicore Device Agent — Graph sending configuration
#
#  Copy as `.env` NEXT TO THE EXECUTABLE (or to
#  %LOCALAPPDATA%\Personicore\DeviceAgent\.env).
#
#  NO .env IS NEEDED. By default the agent works like the router's network.html:
#  it takes the endpoint and jwt from the router (/cgi-bin/get_config.sh), reads
#  the household panelists and SAVES the registration for real.
#  Use this file only to override the endpoint/token or to turn on a dry run.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dry run: true = read the household but send nothing; the registration is
# written to `Personicore-outbox.txt` on the desktop instead. Default: false.
PERSONICORE_DRY_RUN=

# Where the POST goes. Empty = the endpoint served by the router (normal case).
# Stage:  https://graphql.example.invalid/graphql
PERSONICORE_GRAPHQL_ENDPOINT=

# Credential. Empty = use the JWT served by the meter node in get_config.sh,
# which is the normal case: the agent inherits the household credential and
# stores none of its own.
#
# The value is sent VERBATIM as the Authorization header. Nothing is added and
# nothing is stripped: if the endpoint wants "Bearer eyJ...", write the word
# here too. Production does not — the router's JWT goes bare, like
# update_ips_from_graphql.sh and the router's own web page.
PERSONICORE_GRAPHQL_TOKEN=

# Operation name. Only used for the log and the outbox file.
PERSONICORE_GRAPHQL_OPERATION=routerIpsAssigment

# Mutation to use. Empty = the built-in one (routerIpsAssigment).
#
# This overrides the routerIpsAssigment document ONLY. The device mutation
# (presenceCreateDevice, used by registrationMode=device) is not configurable
# from here: its input is one object with required fields the agent derives
# from each other, so a swapped document would not survive the next schema
# change anyway.
#
# IMPORTANT: a custom document must accept exactly these variables, because
# they are the ones the agent builds:
#     $routerId: ID!
#     $addIps: [IPInput!]
#     $removeIps: [RemoveIPAssignmentInput!]
#     $updateIps: [IPInput!]
# What you can change without touching code is which mutation is called and
# which fields it returns.
#
# For a multi-line mutation, point to a file (relative paths are resolved
# next to this .env):
PERSONICORE_GRAPHQL_MUTATION_FILE=

# ...or paste it on one line in double quotes, using \n for line breaks:
# PERSONICORE_GRAPHQL_MUTATION="mutation routerIpsAssigment($routerId: ID!, $addIps: [IPInput!], $removeIps: [RemoveIPAssignmentInput!], $updateIps: [IPInput!]) {\n  routerIpsAssigment(routerId: $routerId, addIps: $addIps, removeIps: $removeIps, updateIps: $updateIps) {\n    id\n    macAddress\n  }\n}"
